    <p>Google may set additional analytics cookies, such as <code>_gid</code>, depending on the tag configuration. Treat any cookie starting with <code>_ga</code> as analytics.</p>

    <h2>Advertising, off until you accept</h2>
    <p>If you accept advertising, the site loads Google Ads tag <code>AW-359263349</code>. The tag is used to measure visits that follow an ad, and to count phone calls as conversions. The conversion label configured for call tracking is <code>AW-359263349/jnwaCIeuh9cZEPXYp6sB</code>, tied to the shop number (702) 333-2463.</p>
    <p>When advertising cookies are on, Google may replace the visible phone number with a forwarding number. The call is still connected to the shop. Google can process the number you call from, the time, and how long the call lasted, so the advertiser can see that an ad led to a call. If advertising cookies are off, the page keeps the real shop number and that swapping does not run.</p>
    <p>A click on a phone link can also send a <code>phone_call_click</code> event to Google when either analytics or advertising is accepted. The event records that a phone link was used. It does not include the truck description from the form.</p>
