    <h2>Requests that are not cookies</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google Fonts.</strong> Every page asks fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com for Barlow Condensed and Work Sans. Your IP address is part of that request. Google says Fonts does not use the request to create ads profiles. See <a href="https://developers.google.com/fonts/faq/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">developers.google.com/fonts/faq/privacy</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>OpenStreetMap tiles.</strong> Only the Service Areas page requests map images from tile.openstreetmap.org. Your IP address is sent so the images can be returned. We do not send the contact form with that request. Policy: <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Global Privacy Control</h2>
    <p>If your browser sends the Global Privacy Control signal and you have not already made an explicit choice on this device, we store a rejection of analytics and advertising cookies and we do not load Google’s tag. An Accept you click yourself is stored as your choice and is followed on later visits, including if the signal is still on. <button type="button" class="text-button" data-action="cookie-consent#optOutShare">Do not sell or share my personal information</button> turns both categories off again and replaces that choice.</p>
    <p>California and Colorado treat a valid Global Privacy Control signal as an opt-out of sale and of sharing for targeted advertising. We apply it to the advertising cookies and, on this site, to analytics cookies as well.</p>

    <h2>How to change your mind</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use Cookie settings in the footer, or the Do not sell or share link, which turns analytics and advertising off.</li>
      <li>Clear cookies and site data for trucksofnevada.com in your browser. That removes the session cookie, the saved choice, and first-party Google cookies such as <code>_ga</code> and <code>_gcl_au</code>. You will see the banner again.</li>
      <li>Cookies set on Google’s own domains, such as <code>IDE</code>, have to be cleared in your browser’s Google or third-party cookie controls. Rejecting on this site stops us from asking Google to set new ones. It cannot reach into Google’s domain and delete an old one.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Browser help pages cover the mechanics: <a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chrome</a>, <a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Safari</a>, <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/kb/clear-cookies-and-site-data-firefox" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firefox</a>, and <a href="https://support.microsoft.com/microsoft-edge/delete-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-63947406-40ac-c3b8-57b9-2a946a29ae09" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Edge</a>.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If we add a new non-essential cookie or a new advertising tag, we will update this page, change the effective date, and ask again before that tag runs.</p>
